<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The wide grid: the expense/income selector over four labelled columns.

    Five rows of four cells, all declared, because RemoteViews has no way to add
    a view at bind time - the renderer shows the cells the size actually has
    room for (WidgetLayout.rows) and hides the rest. The repetition is
    mechanical and the ids are consumed by index in WidgetRenderer.

    Every tinted surface is an ImageView behind its content rather than a
    background on the container: setColorFilter is the only tint a RemoteViews
    can apply, and it only reaches an ImageView. The shapes are solid white, so
    the SRC_ATOP filter reproduces the colour handed to it exactly - which is
    also why WidgetPalette pre-blends its washes instead of sending alpha.
-->
